{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler JQL builders (fetcher.py)","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status = \"Done\"","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","active-set scoping","status category","workflow","Jira","closed-equivalent status"],"propositions":["The reconciler active-set query hardcodes status != \"Done\" which fails to exclude custom closed-equivalent statuses (Closed, Resolved, Cancelled) common in client Jira workflows.","jql_active incorrectly includes issues in Done-category statuses other than literal \"Done\", pulling resolved issues into the active working set where outbound mutations may be applied.","jql_done_recent fails to capture issues in non-Done-literal statuses, creating incomplete recent-Done snapshots.","Switching from literal status = \"Done\" to statusCategory = \"Done\" / statusCategory != \"Done\" makes the active-set scoping workflow-agnostic and covers all custom statuses that map to Jira's Done category.","The fix preserves per-project scoping, single/multi-project fan-out behavior, and DIG/REB workflow equivalence while correctly excluding Done-category statuses in active queries."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787800332757603001,"uuid":"9609f0b6-d9e9-4c28-b960-7b3ddd1539b2"}